Accept browser, promise and image drags, not only Finder file lists

This change applies to crates/gpui_macos/src/window.rs of
zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
(here: src/window.rs on the verbatim 90d8514 tree), after the objc2
start_external_drag migration (72c53bf).

What it does:
- registerForDraggedTypes: public.file-url, public.url, PNG and TIFF data
  and the file-promise types (com.apple.pasteboard.promised-file-url,
  com.apple.filepromise, NSFilesPromisePboardType) alongside
  NSFilenamesPboardType.
- external_paths_from_event: legacy Finder list first (it is the only
  representation that carries several paths); then promised files are
  fulfilled into a temporary directory; then a single public.file-url;
  then an http(s) public.url passed through ExternalPaths as an opaque
  value for the app to download; then raw PNG/TIFF data written to a
  temporary file (512 MiB cap).
- helpers string_from_ns, pasteboard_string, pasteboard_has_type,
  promised_paths, unique_drop_directory and the DROP_SEQUENCE counter.

Three-way on 90d8514: the cocoa import block conflicted with #65361,
which adds NSVisualEffectBlendingMode. Keep the blending mode and the
patch's NSPasteboardTypePNG / NSPasteboardTypeTIFF. Incoming drag
behavior is unchanged. Outgoing start_external_drag stays the objc2
NSDraggingItem path (72c53bf); this patch never owned that function.
UnderWindowBackground (#65361) stays.

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0001-accept-browser-promise-and-image-drags.patch
